[size=5][b]PracticeMode — offline practice mode for STAR WARS: Galactic Racer[/b][/size]
[i](Français plus bas)[/i]

Train on [b]any track[/b] with [b]any vehicle, racer and build[/b], restart instantly, and use [b]save states[/b] to drill the hard sections — fully offline, without ever touching multiplayer or the leaderboards.

[size=4][b]What's new in 2.0.1[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Works again with the current Steam client[/b] (Steam changed how it stores the offline mode: 2.0.0 refused to start)
[/list]

[size=4][b]What's new in 2.0.0[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Works with the game update of 12 October 2026[/b] (Steam build 25880680) — the previous version refuses to start since that update
[*][b]AI opponents[/b] (up to 11, podracers against podracers) with the story mode [b]difficulties[/b]
[*][b]Racer styles[/b]: each racer's own build, abilities and buffs in one click
[*][b]More stable[/b] and smoother races, new dark interface
[/list]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Any track[/b], any vehicle type (speeder bike, car, skimmer, podracer), any racer, any lap count
[*][b]Part-by-part build[/b]: the 6 stat upgrades (0-10), 4 abilities, crash ability, any affixes (by category, with the in-game descriptions)
[*][b]Unlimited crashes[/b]
[*][b]Instant restart[/b] (F6)
[*][b]Save states[/b]: 3 slots (F7 / F8, Shift, Ctrl) — position, speed and boost; gamepad: D-pad down / right
[*][b]Section timer[/b] after each save state load
[*][b]Lap times saved[/b] to a file (date, track, vehicle, racer, time) + "My times" tab with your records
[*]Window in [b]English or French[/b] (FR / EN switch)
[*][b]AI opponents[/b] (up to 11) and [b]AI difficulty[/b] (Cadet, Pilot, Ace, Champion)
[*][b]Racer styles[/b]: the racer's own build, abilities and buffs
[/list]
[b]Known issues — podracers (fixes in 2.1):[/b] launch from the game's [b]main menu[/b] to race in your pilot's own pod; from inside a race, the time trial event's pod is used, and some pod pilots' abilities are incomplete.

[size=4][b]Offline only — by design[/b][/size]
The game keeps times set offline and uploads them to the online leaderboards later. PracticeMode is built so that [b]no modded time can ever reach the leaderboards[/b]:
[list]
[*]it refuses to start unless [b]Steam is in offline mode[/b] and Steam Cloud is off for the game;
[*]during practice, [b]Windows Firewall blocks the game[/b] (you confirm it with the Windows administrator prompt);
[*]when you close the game, your [b]save is restored exactly as before[/b] (modded times are discarded) and the game is back to [b]100% original[/b];
[*]the mod is [b]locked[/b]: installed by hand, without this protection, it does nothing.
[/list]
PracticeMode itself never connects to the Internet.
[b]Never play multiplayer during a practice session.[/b]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10 / 11, Windows Firewall on
[*]Steam version of the game, [b]current version (Steam build 25880680, update of 12 October 2026)[/b] — after a game update, PracticeMode refuses to start until it is updated
[*]Nothing else: [b]UE4SS is included[/b] (with the fixes this game needs) and the window is a standalone .exe
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation & use[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Extract the [i]PracticeMode[/i] folder anywhere except Program Files and the game folder (e.g. C:\PracticeMode).
[*]Steam → [i]Go Offline…[/i] — and untick Steam Cloud in the game's properties.
[*]Run [b]PracticeMode.exe[/b] (unsigned: "More info" → "Run anyway"), click [b]Start practice[/b], accept the administrator prompt.
[*]In the game's main menu, the window fills in: pick track, vehicle, racer, build → [b]Start the race[/b].
[*]Close the game: everything is restored automatically. Put Steam back online.
[/list]
Full guide: README.txt / LISEZMOI.txt in the archive (including exactly what the launcher does).

